# phases.expected - the phase->destination roster (F38, F41).
#
# The conservation gate asserts that carve-map.tsv's `phase` column induces
# EXACTLY this grouping. Re-ordering the Phase-5 commits therefore means editing
# a promise a reviewer reads, not a cell nobody re-reads.
#
# Phases 2-4 land as one commit each and carry whole ordinals. Phase 5 is DEFINED
# as six commits (F22), so its ordinals are decimal (5.1..5.6) and `--phase 5.N`
# is green at each of the six (F41). Ordering is numeric, so the comparison is total.
#
# Rows here: 9. Destinations here: 13 (the content destinations). `agents/mozart.md`
# has no row - its ranges carry phase 0 and never move, which is what Control 3's
# inverse direction asserts. `agents/INDEX.md` has no row - it holds no PRE lines
# and is not in the partition set (F7/F33); it is gated separately.
#
# ordinal	destinations (comma-separated, sorted)
2	agents/AUDIT.md,agents/CONTEXT-BUDGET.md,agents/DIAGNOSE.md,agents/EVAL.md
3	agents/INCIDENT.md,agents/OPERATE.md
4	agents/STATE.md
5.1	agents/INTAKE.md
5.2	agents/COUNTERPOINT.md
5.3	agents/FLOWS.md
5.4	agents/WORKTREES.md
5.5	agents/TICKETS.md
5.6	agents/DELIVER.md
